#
# WHY THIS FILE STILL EXISTS, and why it is named like a hazard instead of like
# a default. It is the only way to reproduce something that depends on the real
# corpus — 150 live drafts, a connector's actual output, a customer's exact
# scope tree. That is a narrow, deliberate, READ-ONLY errand, and it was the
# ONLY local env this repo shipped until bd startsim-768w.69, which meant
# "run it locally" and "drive a paying customer's production data" were the same
# sentence. It was called `.env.local.variantA`, and `cp .env.local.variantA
# .env.local` is a thing a person — or an agent told to "test it locally" —
# does without reading a header. The name is now one nobody copies by accident.
#
# USING IT, if you have decided you must:
#   1. Read, do not write. A delete here deletes a customer's record.
#   2. It expects a local proxy on :4015 that forwards to the tenant with the
#      right Host header; DJANGO_API_URL below is that proxy, not the tenant.
#   3. cp .env.variantA.PRODUCTION-TENANT .env.local   (and delete it after)
#
